# Canonical Git remote

- **Only** commit and push work to this repository:
  - `https://github.com/abbieymatthewslol/abbiey-search-engine.git`
  - SSH equivalent: `git@github.com:abbieymatthewslol/abbiey-search-engine.git`
- Do **not** add alternate `origin` URLs, push to other remotes, or suggest deploying from a fork unless the user explicitly asks to change remotes.
- Default branch for releases/CI in this repo is **`master`** (see `.github/workflows/`). Keep `main` in sync when the user cares about Vercel Git integration; do not invent a different upstream.
- When running `git push`, use `origin` (no ad-hoc remotes). If `origin` is wrong, fix it with:
  `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/abbieymatthewslol/abbiey-search-engine.git`

Optional local guard (if enabled): `core.hooksPath` → `.githooks` runs `pre-push` to block pushes when `origin` is not this repo.
